    12	// Checkpoints do not necessarily sync to a remote named "origin". The CLI
    13	// elects ONE remote to carry them — strategy_options.checkpoint_push_remote,
    14	// then a remote a past push captured, then "origin", then the sole/first remote
    15	// in .git/config order — and its read paths consult that elected remote first
    16	// with "origin" behind it as a legacy tier
    17	// (cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_read_remotes.go). The export reader looked
    18	// only at the local branch and origin's tracking ref, so a clone whose elected
    19	// remote is named anything else had checkpoints the brain never saw.
